- `Expense(id, householdId, date, amount, storeId?, category, source[MANUAL|RECEIPT], receiptId?)`
- `WasteLog(id, productId, qtyBase, cost, reason, date)`
- `Task(id, householdId, title, dueAt?, assignee?, status, kind[SHOPPING|CHORE|REMINDER])`
- `BabyProfile(id, profileId, birthDate, diapersPerDay, size, weightKg?)` / `DiaperLog(...)`

### IA y plataforma
- `AiInteraction(id, householdId, memberId, capability, model, promptHash, tokensIn, tokensOut, costEstimate, latencyMs, status, createdAt)`
- `Notification(id, householdId, memberId, kind, payload, scheduledAt, deliveredAt, readAt)`
- `Entitlement(id, householdId, sku, status, purchaseToken, verifiedAt, expiresAt?, source)`
- `Outbox(id, entity, entityId, op, payload, deviceId, createdAt, syncedAt?)`
- `AuditLog(id, householdId, actorId, action, entity, entityId, before, after, at)`

**Reglas de integridad:**
- `qtyBase >= 0` siempre; ajustes negativos requieren motivo.
- Un movimiento con el mismo `idempotencyKey` no se aplica dos veces.
- Borrar un producto no borra su historial: se marca `archived`.
- `Expense` de una factura se genera desde la misma captura que creó los movimientos.

